{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790973427,"nonce":"XwILzF+QxaT4W2agMZAXaIC2zLQ=","title":"rank is a built-in field on every type, null until a drag writes it","message":"Decided 2026-10-02 (Luis): `rank` joins `title`, `type` and `archived` as a built-in, present on every type and unremovable, because Jira and Linear both put an order on every issue and every type in the preset carried it anyway. It is nullable and starts null: `new` writes none, the first drag does, and null sorts after every set rank, ties by id. Views default their `rank` argument to the built-in, so Space on an id, a card or a bar always grabs; the argument stays for a second ordering. The default `git work issue` listing stays last-edited first.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["issue-model","tui","cli"],"priority":"high","status":"in-progress","type":"decision"}}]}